1 Overview
**********

Runes aims to do FreeType's job of loading fonts and serving their
metrics, and fontconfig's job of discovering and caching them, without
calling into foreign libraries.  The aim is similar to Google's
Fontations.  It is developed and tested on SBCL.

* Menu:

* Systems::                     Systems, packages and licenses.
* Requirements::                What each system depends on.


File: runes.info,  Node: Systems,  Next: Requirements,  Up: Overview

1.1 Systems
===========

‘runes’
     Package ‘RUNES’, nicknames ‘TRUETYPE’ and ‘CL-TRUETYPE’; in
     ‘src/core/’.  The font manager: font discovery, the ‘font’ class,
     open font loaders, metrics, and glyph positions along a line.  It
     draws and rasterizes nothing and depends on no graphics library.
     *Note Font manager::.

‘runes/raster’
     Package ‘RUNES/RASTER’; in ‘src/raster/’.  Rasterizes strings and
     single glyphs to 8-bit alpha maps with cl-vectors and cl-aa.  *Note
     Rasterizer::.

‘runes/raster-antron’
     The same package and API as ‘runes/raster’, rasterizing with
     Antron's CPU rasterizer instead of cl-vectors and cl-aa.  Load one
     of the two, not both.

‘runes/xcb’
     Package ‘RUNES/XCB’, nicknames ‘RUNES-XCB’, ‘XCB-TRUETYPE’ and
     ‘XFT’; in ‘src/xcb/’.  Draws text on X11 through XCB and RENDER
     glyph sets, and re-exports the ‘RUNES’ and ‘RUNES/RASTER’ API.
     *Note X11 bridge::.

‘runes/wayland’
     Package ‘RUNES/WAYLAND’; in ‘src/wayland/’.  Draws text into pixels
     the client owns, as on Wayland.  *Note Client-side bridge::.

‘zpb-ttf’
     Package ‘ZPB-TTF’; sources in ‘otf/src/’.  The zpb-ttf font loader
     API, kept so that zpb-ttf programs work unchanged, on top of
     ‘runes/otf’.  BSD 2-Clause.  *Note Font loader::.

‘runes/otf’
     Package ‘RUNES/OTF’, nickname ‘OTF’; in ‘otf/’.  Bounds-checked
     readers for about 50 OpenType tables, generated from schemas, plus
     WOFF and WOFF2 decoding.  MIT. *Note OpenType tables::.

‘runes/otf/charstring’
     Package ‘RUNES/OTF/CHARSTRING’.  The CFF and CFF2 charstring
     interpreter and DICT parser, a port of Fontations'.  MIT. *Note CFF
     charstrings::.

‘decompress’
     Package ‘DECOMPRESS’; in ‘decompress/’.  Brotli, zlib and raw
     deflate decoders with no dependencies.  MIT. *Note Decompression::.

   For backward compatibility, ‘cl-truetype.asd’ loads ‘runes’ and
‘runes/raster’, and ‘clxcb-truetype.asd’ loads ‘runes/xcb’.

   Antron renders text from ‘runes’ alone: it takes fonts, metrics and
layout from it and rasterizes the outlines itself, so it does not need
‘runes/raster’ or a bridge.


File: runes.info,  Node: Requirements,  Prev: Systems,  Up: Overview

1.2 Requirements
================

   • SBCL. ‘runes’ and the bridges use portable libraries and may work
     elsewhere, untested; ‘runes/otf’, ‘zpb-ttf’ and ‘decompress’ use
     SBCL internals and need SBCL.
   • ASDF 3 and UIOP.
   • cacle, for the LFU caches of string metrics and alpha maps, and
     bordeaux-threads, for the locks around font loaders and caches.
   • ‘runes/raster’: cl-vectors, cl-paths-ttf and cl-aa, and
     trivial-garbage.  ‘runes/raster-antron’: Antron instead of the
     cl-vectors libraries.
   • ‘runes/xcb’: clxcb, the XCB binding.

   With the sb-simd-512 build of SBCL (with AVX-512), parts of
‘decompress’ use AVX-512.  Stock SBCL runs the plain Lisp code; check
for ‘:decompress-avx512’ in ‘*features*’.


