3.1 The font cache
==================

 -- Variable: *font-dirs*
     The directories searched for fonts.  By default
     ‘/usr/share/fonts/’, ‘/usr/local/share/fonts/’,
     ‘~/.local/share/fonts/’ and ‘~/.fonts/’, and on macOS also
     ‘/Library/Fonts/’ and ‘/System/Library/Fonts/’.

 -- Variable: *font-cache*
     A hash table of family name to a hash table of subfamily name to
     pathname.  Guarded by a lock.

 -- Function: cache-fonts
     Scan ‘*font-dirs*’ for ‘.ttf’ files and replace ‘*font-cache*’ with
     what is found.  The scan builds a new table and swaps it in when
     done, so other threads go on finding fonts meanwhile.  Call it once
     per image, and again after installing fonts.  Only files with the
     type ‘ttf’ are indexed, although the loader also opens ‘.otf’,
     ‘.ttc’, ‘.woff’ and ‘.woff2’ files given by pathname.

 -- Function: cache-font-file pathname
     Add the font in PATHNAME to ‘*font-cache*’.  A file the loader
     cannot read is skipped.

 -- Function: get-font-families
     Return the list of cached family names.

 -- Function: get-font-subfamilies family
     Return the subfamilies of FAMILY, such as ‘Regular’, ‘Italic’ or
     ‘Bold’.

 -- Function: check-valid-font-families family subfamily
     Signal an error unless FAMILY and SUBFAMILY are in the cache,
     calling ‘cache-fonts’ first if the cache is empty.

 -- Function: get-font-pathname font
     Return the pathname of the file FONT is read from.


