3.2 Fonts
=========

 -- Class: font family subfamily size underline strikethrough overline
          antialias background foreground overwrite-gcontext
     A face, a size and a text style.  Make one with

          (make-instance 'font :family "DejaVu Sans" :subfamily "Book" :size 24)

     SIZE is in pixels.  SUBFAMILY may be omitted or ‘nil’; then
     Regular, Book, or the first available subfamily is used.
     UNDERLINE, STRIKETHROUGH and OVERLINE default to false, ANTIALIAS
     to true.  BACKGROUND, FOREGROUND and OVERWRITE-GCONTEXT are kept
     from clx-truetype and not used by the bridges, which take the
     colour as an argument.

 -- Accessor: font-family font
 -- Accessor: font-subfamily font
 -- Accessor: font-size font
 -- Accessor: font-underline font
 -- Accessor: font-strikethrough font
 -- Accessor: font-overline font
 -- Accessor: font-antialias font
 -- Accessor: font-background font
 -- Accessor: font-foreground font
 -- Accessor: font-overwrite-gcontext font
     The font's slots.  Setting one flushes the font's caches, so a font
     can be reconfigured and reused.

 -- Generic Function: font-equal font1 font2
     True if the two fonts have the same family, subfamily and size, and
     the same value in every style slot.

 -- Generic Function: flush-font-caches font
     Flush everything cached for FONT.  A renderer that caches images
     per font adds an ‘:after’ method to flush those too, as
     ‘runes/raster’ does.

 -- Accessor: font-string-bboxes font
 -- Accessor: font-string-line-bboxes font
     The font's caches of string bounding boxes.

 -- Function: make-font-cache font dpi-cache-size string-cache-size
          inner-provider
 -- Function: font-cache-fetch cache dpi string
     A two-level cache, per DPI and then per string, of values computed
     by INNER-PROVIDER.  Used for the bounding box caches.


File: runes.info,  Node: Font loaders,  Next: Targets and DPI,  Prev: Fonts,  Up: Font manager

3.3 Font loaders
================

Each font file is opened once, by the zpb-ttf loader (*note Font
loader::), and the loader is kept open for the life of the image.

 -- Variable: *font-loader-cache*
     A hash table of pathname to open font loader.

 -- Macro: with-font-loader (loader font) &body body
     Run BODY with LOADER bound to FONT's cached loader, opening it the
     first time, while holding the font loader lock.  A loader is not
     thread-safe, so use it only inside this macro.

 -- Function: close-font-loaders
     Close every cached loader and empty ‘*font-loader-cache*’.


