3.4 Targets and DPI
===================

The metric functions take a “target”, which gives the resolution the
text is measured at: an integer DPI, a cons ‘(DPI-X . DPI-Y)’, or, with
a bridge loaded, a drawable or a screen.  Anything else counts as 96
DPI.

 -- Generic Function: target-dpi target
     Return ‘(values DPI-X DPI-Y)’ for TARGET.  A backend adds methods
     for its own drawables and screens.

 -- Function: font-units->pixels-x dpi-x font
 -- Function: font-units->pixels-y dpi-y font
     Return the factor that converts font units to pixels.


File: runes.info,  Node: Metrics,  Next: Layout,  Prev: Targets and DPI,  Up: Font manager

3.5 Metrics
===========

All lengths are in pixels.  The “bounding box” of a string is its ink:
the box around the glyphs as drawn.  The “line box” spans the advance
widths horizontally and the font's ascent and descent vertically, which
is what lines laid out one under another need.

 -- Function: font-ascent target font
 -- Function: font-descent target font
 -- Function: font-line-gap target font
 -- Function: baseline-to-baseline target font
     The font's ascent, descent (negative, as in TrueType), line gap,
     and the distance between the baselines of two lines.

 -- Function: font-ascent-for-dpi dpi-y font
 -- Function: font-descent-for-dpi dpi-y font
     The same as ‘font-ascent’ and ‘font-descent’, for a DPI.

 -- Function: font-lines-height target font lines-count
     The height of LINES-COUNT lines: ascent plus descent for one line,
     plus the line gap between lines.

 -- Function: text-bounding-box target font string &key start end
 -- Function: text-width target font string &key start end
 -- Function: text-height target font string &key start end
     The bounding box of STRING, from START to END, and its width and
     height.

 -- Function: text-line-bounding-box target font string &key start end
 -- Function: text-line-width target font string &key start end
 -- Function: text-line-height target font string &key start end
     The same for the line box.

 -- Function: xmin bounding-box
 -- Function: ymin bounding-box
 -- Function: xmax bounding-box
 -- Function: ymax bounding-box
     The sides of a bounding box.

 -- Variable: *allow-fixed-pitch-p*
     When true, the default, the width of a line in a font marked
     fixed-pitch is the first glyph's advance times the length.  Faster,
     but wrong for fonts whose CJK glyphs are double width despite the
     flag; bind it to ‘nil’ for those.


File: runes.info,  Node: Layout,  Next: Fitting and centring,  Prev: Metrics,  Up: Font manager

3.6 Layout
==========

 -- Function: layout-string font string &key (dpi-x 96) (letter-spacing
          0.0) (word-spacing 0.0) kerning-table
     Lay out STRING on one line.  LETTER-SPACING is added after each
     character, WORD-SPACING after each space.  Kerning comes from
     KERNING-TABLE or else from the font.  Return ‘(values LAYOUT
     TOTAL-ADVANCE)’, where LAYOUT is a vector of ‘(GLYPH-INDEX PEN-X)’,
     PEN-X the exact pen position in pixels from the start of the line.

 -- Function: kern-offset font char1 char2 &key custom-table (dpi-x 96)
     The kerning between CHAR1 and CHAR2 in fractional pixels, from
     CUSTOM-TABLE if given, else from the font.

 -- Function: line-box font dpi &key (multiplier 1.0) explicit-height
     Return ‘(values ASCENT DESCENT HEIGHT LEADING)’ in pixels, ASCENT
     and DESCENT both positive.  HEIGHT is the natural line height times
     MULTIPLIER, or EXPLICIT-HEIGHT.

 -- Function: font-decorations font string x y dpi-x dpi-y line-p
     The underline, strikethrough and overline of STRING drawn at
     baseline (X, Y), as a list of rectangles ‘(LEFT TOP WIDTH HEIGHT)’,
     y down.  They span the bounding box, or the line box when LINE-P.
     ‘nil’ when the font has none of the three set.


File: runes.info,  Node: Fitting and centring,  Prev: Layout,  Up: Font manager

3.7 Fitting and centring
========================

 -- Function: fit-font target family subfamily string box-width
          box-height &key (min-size 8) (probe-size 100)
     Return a new font of FAMILY and SUBFAMILY, as large as possible
     with STRING's line box inside BOX-WIDTH by BOX-HEIGHT, and at least
     MIN-SIZE.

 -- Function: fit-font-size target family subfamily string box-width
          box-height &key (min-size 8) (probe-size 100)
     Like ‘fit-font’, but return only the size, for a caller that
     resizes a font of its own.

 -- Function: text-center target font string box-width box-height
     Return ‘(values BASELINE-X BASELINE-Y)’ that centre STRING in a box
     of BOX-WIDTH by BOX-HEIGHT, to pass to ‘draw-text-line’.


