8.2 Table readers
=================

The table readers are generated from s-expression schemas in
‘otf/schemas/’, derived from the Fontations table definitions, by the
code generator in ‘otf/codegen/’; the generated code is in
‘otf/src/tables/’.  To change a reader, change its schema or the
generator and run ‘make codegen’.  Every table follows the same naming:

‘(read-TABLE FONT-DATA OFFSET &optional LENGTH)’
     Check the table's fixed part and return a view of it, a structure
     named TABLE.  For example ‘read-head’, ‘read-hhea’, ‘read-cmap’.
‘(TABLE-FIELD VIEW)’
     A field, decoded.  ‘(head-units-per-em head)’.
‘(TABLE-FIELD-raw FONT-DATA OFFSET)’
     The same field read straight from the bytes, without a view.
‘(TABLE-ARRAY-count VIEW)’
‘(TABLE-ARRAY-ref VIEW INDEX)’
     The length and the elements of an array field.
‘(FLAGS-FLAG-p FLAGS)’
     A bit of a flags field.
‘+TABLE-tag+’
‘+RECORD-size+’
     The table's tag and the size of a fixed record, as constants.

   Every view includes ‘table-ref’ (with ‘table-ref-font-data’,
‘table-ref-offset’, ‘table-ref-length’), and every record ‘record-ref’.
Offsets inside a table are followed with ‘resolve-offset16’,
‘resolve-offset32’ and their ‘nullable’ versions.

   The tables of a font are found through its table directory:

     (let* ((fd (otf:ensure-font-data #p"DejaVuSans.ttf"))
            (td (otf:read-table-directory fd 0)))
       (dotimes (i (otf:table-directory-table-records-count td))
         (let ((rec (otf:table-directory-table-records-ref td i)))
           (when (string= (otf:table-record-tag rec) "head")
             (return (otf:head-units-per-em
                      (otf:read-head fd (otf:table-record-offset rec)
                                     (otf:table-record-length rec))))))))

   A collection starts with a ‘ttc-header’ instead (‘read-ttc-header’),
whose ‘ttc-header-table-directory-offsets-ref’ gives each font's table
directory.

   Tables with readers include the core TrueType tables (‘head’, ‘hhea’,
‘hmtx’, ‘maxp’, ‘name’, ‘OS/2’, ‘post’, ‘cmap’, ‘glyf’, ‘kern’), the
layout tables (‘GDEF’, ‘GSUB’, ‘GPOS’, ‘BASE’, ‘MATH’), the variation
tables (‘fvar’, ‘avar’, ‘gvar’, ‘cvar’, ‘HVAR’, ‘VVAR’, ‘MVAR’, ‘STAT’),
colour and bitmap tables (‘COLR’, ‘CPAL’, ‘CBDT’, ‘CBLC’, ‘EBDT’,
‘EBLC’, ‘sbix’, ‘SVG ’) and the Apple tables (‘morx’, ‘kerx’, ‘feat’,
‘trak’, ‘ankr’ and others).  ‘otf/doc/font-loader-details.md’ lists them
and the tables left out.

   A few layouts whose shape depends on the data itself are decoded by
hand in ‘otf/src/extensions.lisp’, for example ‘fvar-axis-ref’,
‘fvar-instance-ref’, ‘gvar-glyph-variation-data-header’,
‘read-gpos-value-record’, ‘pair-set-pair-value-record-ref’,
‘mvar-value-record-ref’ and ‘strike-glyph-data’.  Their docstrings
describe them.


