10 Decompression
****************

The ‘decompress’ system, package ‘DECOMPRESS’, decodes Brotli (RFC
7932), zlib (RFC 1950) and raw deflate (RFC 1951) data held in memory.
It has no dependencies and works on its own.  It neither streams nor
compresses.  The input is read in place.

 -- Function: decompress input &key size-hint (start 0) end
     Decode the Brotli stream in INPUT, an octet vector, between START
     and END, and return the decoded octets.  SIZE-HINT, the decoded
     size if known (WOFF2 records it), lets the output be allocated
     once.

 -- Function: zlib-decompress input &key size-hint (start 0) end
 -- Function: inflate input &key size-hint (start 0) end
     Decode a zlib stream (header, deflate data, Adler-32), or raw
     deflate data, in the same way.

 -- Condition: decompression-error
 -- Condition: brotli-error
 -- Condition: deflate-error
     Malformed input.  ‘brotli-error’ and ‘deflate-error’ are subtypes
     of ‘decompression-error’.

   The Brotli decoder needs the Brotli dictionary,
‘decompress/data/dictionary.bin’, read the first time a stream uses it.
An image saved with ‘save-lisp-and-die’ should load it first.

   ‘decompress/README.md’ has the measurements against libbrotli,
zlib-ng and libdeflate, and ‘decompress/doc/optimizations.md’ records
what was tried.


